this is what we're here for  the brand new dual sense controller so  on first impressions  just looking at the controller it is not  as bright white as i thought it was  going to be from all the marketing and  everything we've seen at the playstation  5 so far  i genuinely thought this was going to be  a bright white it actually has more of a  grayish  tinge to it when you're looking at it uh  in real life so  first impressions it feels really nice  in the hand it feels very familiar if  you've been playing  on a dualshock 4 a lot it just feels a  bit sturdier a little bit heavier  let's start with the charging port we've  already seen the charging cable usb  c it's right at the back there in terms  of the face buttons  they have lost all their color probably  to fit in with this new sleek black and  white  look so shoulder buttons there's a  little more sound feedback when you're  pressing them which actually feels quite  nice they feel like way more responsive  i don't know if it's just because my  dual shock 4 is quite old and it feels a  little bit sticky the face buttons are  actually  a lot softer to press and actually the  touchpad has more of a feedback in it as  well the  dualshock 4 touchpad felt very very soft  to me but this one feels like it's  way more of a button but the face  buttons themselves do feel a lot softer  to press  the thumbsticks have rubber textures on  them  they feel pretty good they actually feel  a little bit firmer the playstation home  button has been replaced it used to be a  circular button  now it's just the playstation logo but  obviously it's actually quite it's  hidden quite well in there so  you're probably not going to hit that  accidentally beneath that  is another button so you can use the  dual sense controller as a microphone  seeing videos and pictures of people in  party chat and using  the dual sense to either do  text-to-speech when they're talking to  their friends and messaging them  or you can use it as a microphone so  this is a button to turn your microphone  on and off if you don't want to use that  feature  beneath it you have a headphone jack  where you can plug in just your regular  headset  if you have an old headset that you're  plugging in you want to use it as a  microphone or just for the headphones  you can plug  it in there it also has kind of a  texturized  plastic on the back so you don't feel  like you're going to drop it it's not  smooth  like the dual shark it feels nice it  feels weighty the options button is now  gone it no longer says options  instead you have this button here which  serves as a replacement  word options is gone you just got the  three lines and on the other side the  share button is gone  this time around it's the create button  uh it has  three lines going in different direction  but this is the button you would hit to  take screenshots  video clips and then mark them up and  share them with your friends
 

